 "superseded_2026-11-13_b118": {
  "reason": "B-118 step 2 (code review of 13 Nov 2026): the values published before the dtn.py fixes. N3: a store-and-forward bundle got a full set of transmissions in every step whatever time was left and its lifetime was checked only at the step's start, so grants could be delivered up to about 40 s late and counted delivered; an arrival on a step's last transmission was stamped at the next step. N4: bundles still alive at the window's end were counted lost (now 'censored'). N5: age of information was floored at dt/2 = 30 s. N6: the lost-link return used the driving time in the hour before the loss, which no text describes (now as the papers state it). C11: a relay's store limit was not checked on forwarding (no queue came near 64 MB, so no value moved by it). Kept as published, with the B-111 v0.2 block.",
